-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 66 DOWN: no-op.
--
-- Migration 66 is a self-healing schema repair: it re-asserts the canonical
-- `mentions` TYPE RELATION FROM source TO entity definition (the shape the
-- ontology always intended; the physical table had drifted to TYPE ANY
-- SCHEMALESS). There is no faithful inverse —
--   * reverting `mentions` to TYPE ANY would re-break `RELATE source ->
--     mentions -> entity` and is exactly the drift 66 exists to fix; and
--   * `mentions` is a DERIVED projection of `entity.source_documents` (Track
--     U.2) — the canonical data lives in the entity rows, so the edge table can
--     be regenerated at will and has no state worth a destructive rollback.
-- Down intentionally does nothing; mirrors migration 62's down convention.
-- ============================================================================
